# Editor-only configuration for clangd. Builds are governed by
# cmake/TinyioWarnings.cmake; this file exists because clangd replays the
# compile database verbatim and does not re-run CMake.
#
# Why -Wno-c2y-extensions: newer clangd (Homebrew ships 23.x) classifies
# __COUNTER__ as a C2y extension, and the -Wpedantic carried by the compile
# database turns that into a squiggle on every TRY/TRY_VOID expansion site
# (the diagnostic fires where the macro EXPANDS, in every translation unit,
# so it cannot be pragma-suppressed at the definition in error.hpp). The
# pinned toolchain clang (20) does not have the diagnostic at all, and
# TinyioWarnings.cmake adds the matching -Wno- for toolchains that do; this
# covers the editor in between.
CompileFlags:
  Add: [-Wno-c2y-extensions]
